[00:28.16] Southern trees bear strange fruit,
[00:34.36] Blood on the leaves and blood at the root,
[00:42.54] Black bodies swinging in the southern breeze,
[00:50.60] Strange fruit hanging from the poplar trees.
[00:58.76] Pastoral scene of the gallant south,
[01:06.91] Of the bulging eyes and the twisted mouth,
[01:15.07] Scent of magnolias, sweet and fresh,
[01:22.23] Then the sudden smell of burning flesh.
[02:40.98] Here is fruit for the crows to pluck,
[02:48.11] For the rain to gather, for the wind to suck,
[02:56.24] For the sun to rot, for the trees to drop,
[03:05.32] Here is a strange and bitter crop
[03:18.91] 